re.md:236-240 retains that narrow exception. check_consumer_graph.py:40-45 mechanically rejects this precise non-sc-cron introducing edge; ci.yml:124-127 invokes it. Existing .triage/c/findings/RBQA-F001.ttl remains open. Correlates ARCH-001, not a new defect ID.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-sync/Cargo.toml\", \"id\": \"RBQA-F001\", \"issue\": \"The inherited sync crate directly depends on sc-command below the isolated Python consumer, exceeding ADR-BDC-0016 decision 5's exception for upstream published sc-cron only.\", \"justification_check\": \"Missing requirement/ADR justification\", \"line\": 31, \"recommendation\": \"Keep the owning C1/upstream correction open. Preserve canonical scheduler logging through a published upstream logging facade, then remove this direct dependency and qualify the isolated normal/build consumer graph. Do not relax the ADR or the guard.\", \"related_artifacts\": [\"docs/architecture.md#adr-bdc-0016-adopt-the-sc-runtime-application-framework-and-scheduler\", \"docs/bd-cache-py/architecture.md\", \"docs/bd-cache-api/requirements.md\", \"crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron_log.rs\", \"crates/bd-cache-sync/tests/check_consumer_graph.py\", \".github/workflows/ci.yml\", \".triage/c/findings/RBQA-F001.ttl\"], \"reviewer\": \"ruthless-boundary-qa\", \"severity\": \"critical\"}], \"severity\": \"critical\"}" .
